WEBVTT

00:05.080 --> 00:08.170
Spirits, oh my Spirits...

00:11.710 --> 00:18.250
Deliver the divine message of
Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto to her miko, dear Spirits...

00:38.540 --> 00:40.630
Miko, oh miko...

00:41.380 --> 00:45.580
Get combo bonus number 3...
you will choose number 3...

00:51.380 --> 00:57.920
Miko, oh miko... on the way home,
buy the limited edition cola from Fuji Mart.

01:02.460 --> 01:03.500
Oh, miko...

01:05.000 --> 01:09.210
...there is a new game releasing this month,
so can I get an advance on my offerings?

01:13.210 --> 01:14.500
Miko...

01:17.080 --> 01:22.540
...I don't know this crossword hint...
It's 5 characters and ends in "ku."

01:25.830 --> 01:29.290
Miko, oh miko...

01:31.330 --> 01:37.170
Miko... Miko, oh miko...

03:09.040 --> 03:13.710
<b>EPISODE 5</b>

03:09.040 --> 03:13.710
<b>TSUKISHIMA GIRLS'</b>

03:09.040 --> 03:13.710
<b>COLLECTION</b>

03:10.290 --> 03:12.420
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

03:12.790 --> 03:17.170
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

03:18.080 --> 03:24.540
The goddess summoned from another world
enshrined here... was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

03:25.540 --> 03:27.960
A-are you okay, spirits?

03:28.290 --> 03:32.130
Sorry... I guess I've sent too many divine messages.

03:32.460 --> 03:34.080
You call those "divine messages"?

03:35.670 --> 03:38.080
Must be so hard on you. Want some tea?

03:41.000 --> 03:45.290
Poor thing. Hey, Elda, you need a smartphone.

03:45.290 --> 03:47.710
That way the Spirits can get some rest.

03:50.330 --> 03:54.080
What does that face mean?
Elda, you like electronic devices, don't you?

03:54.420 --> 03:59.960
U-uh, no, I don't want one. Th-there's something
anxiety-inducing about a phone, you know?

04:00.170 --> 04:02.500
If you don't like making calls,
how about sending instant messages?

04:02.880 --> 04:05.380
Instant messages? What exactly
are we "mess"ing up so fast?

04:04.290 --> 04:05.040
<b>Mess?</b>

04:05.630 --> 04:09.830
Not that, I mean like a text message. See, like this.

04:10.290 --> 04:12.210
How is this different from an email?

04:12.460 --> 04:14.170
Texts are way cooler.

04:14.330 --> 04:16.290
Then it's basically a cool email?

04:16.920 --> 04:18.250
Oh, I know!

04:18.790 --> 04:25.460
Here's a smart phone I used to use.
I was using it to listen to music, but it's yours now.

04:26.830 --> 04:32.670
There's no... SIMA card in there so you can't
use it outside, but you can at least text me.

04:33.210 --> 04:36.210
Um, as long as you're using the, uh... weefee?

04:36.210 --> 04:37.170
That's "wifi."

04:38.210 --> 04:44.130
Hmm, but I'm very reluctant about this.
I've never had a phone before.

04:44.630 --> 04:48.670
Huh? Then how are you
communicating with Yolde-sama?

04:49.000 --> 04:51.460
Like for that Ringmyoro thingy?

04:51.460 --> 04:53.210
It's "Ringberry Bjorling."

04:54.000 --> 05:00.170
My spirits can't fly all the way to Osaka.
In the Edo days I'd ask an express messenger to do it.

05:00.170 --> 05:03.830
I know about those! They're the half-naked people
who run really fast, right?

05:04.210 --> 05:07.920
Yes, but when you describe them like that,
it sounds extremely misleading.

05:08.330 --> 05:12.670
Express messengers were originally,
when Ieyasu-kun founded the Edo shogunate,

05:12.670 --> 05:17.170
put in place because they needed a way to send official
documents back and forth between Kyoto and Edo.

05:17.830 --> 05:20.000
There were several types of express messengers, too.

05:20.210 --> 05:24.880
For the shogunate's official service, important documents
and the like were carried by express relay messengers.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.420
<b>Express Relay Messengers</b>

05:25.420 --> 05:28.420
The feudal lord of various regions
had the "Feudal Lord Messenger."

05:27.080 --> 05:28.290
<b>Feudal Lord Messenger</b>

05:29.000 --> 05:31.130
The common folk had the "Town Messenger."

05:30.250 --> 05:31.330
<b>Town Messenger</b>

05:31.330 --> 05:33.790
<b>NIHOMBASHI</b>

05:31.540 --> 05:34.380
At the post towns along the Tokaido Road,
horseback riders would pass messages,

05:34.380 --> 05:36.170
and it was carried via a type of relay.

05:35.790 --> 05:37.580
<b>SHINAGAWA</b>

05:36.380 --> 05:39.960
Wow. So a messenger didn't do
the whole thing on their own.

05:38.040 --> 05:40.290
<b>KAWASAKI</b>

05:39.710 --> 05:40.290
<b>KANAGAWA</b>

05:40.290 --> 05:46.040
Another duty of the express messenger was
communicating info to each area about natural disasters.

05:46.330 --> 05:51.630
That's why the common folk couldn't use the express
relay messengers that carried important documents.

05:52.290 --> 05:55.540
I would also normally use the the town messenger, but...

05:56.170 --> 06:01.880
for the documents that I absolutely did not want seen,
I asked the shogunate to send it via relay messenger...

06:02.250 --> 06:05.000
D-documents you didn't want seen?

06:05.880 --> 06:10.880
<b>YOLDE</b>

06:05.880 --> 06:10.880
<b>BOUGHT A BOAT FOR SAIL</b>

06:06.960 --> 06:10.580
Like when Yolde and I had a bad pun showdown.

06:10.920 --> 06:12.170
Not bad, Yolde.

06:12.210 --> 06:14.790
"Stinky elephants are smellephants." This round is mine!

06:12.290 --> 06:15.170
<b>STINKY ELEPHANTS</b>

06:12.290 --> 06:15.170
<b>ARE SMELLEPHANTS...</b>

06:15.210 --> 06:18.210
I'd like to apologize to the messengers back then.

06:18.830 --> 06:21.290
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

06:28.080 --> 06:29.920
Give it a try when you feel like it!

06:30.710 --> 06:33.630
A smartphone, huh...?

06:36.920 --> 06:39.630
That screen came on just by touching it!

06:40.250 --> 06:42.330
It... it truly is a smart phone.

06:46.170 --> 06:50.330
Hmm... it's much easier to use than I thought it'd be.

06:50.920 --> 06:55.170
Oh! The masterpiece RPG on the SNES
has been ported to an app.

06:55.170 --> 06:57.580
That one I love so much I've cleared it a million times...

06:59.170 --> 07:01.420
This is the one that was on the console!

07:01.880 --> 07:03.580
I didn't know I could play it on a smartphone!

07:07.920 --> 07:12.380
<b>It's Koito.</b>

07:07.920 --> 07:12.380
<b>Hey there, Elda, did you try out your smartphone?</b>

07:08.080 --> 07:12.000
It's Koito. Hey there, Elda,
did you try out your smartphone?

07:12.710 --> 07:17.540
I-I got an email from Koito...
oh, she called it a "text message," I believe.

07:19.920 --> 07:21.250
It's a Frog Tank!

07:23.080 --> 07:24.750
So those are called stamps!

07:28.380 --> 07:29.500
<b>Surrendered</b>

07:33.290 --> 07:35.670
Ooh, a text from Elda.

07:35.920 --> 07:40.290
Miko, oh miko, smartphones are quite fun.

07:35.920 --> 07:40.380
<b>Miko,</b>

07:35.920 --> 07:40.380
<b>oh miko,</b>

07:35.920 --> 07:40.380
<b>smartphones are quite fun</b>

07:40.540 --> 07:43.460
Wow, Elda has a smartphone, huh?

07:43.830 --> 07:47.790
Her Spirits are out of action right now.
I gave her my old one.

07:55.710 --> 07:57.670
<b>Koito</b>

07:55.710 --> 07:57.670
<b>1 message</b>

07:57.670 --> 07:59.420
Sh-she replied!

08:02.420 --> 08:07.130
<b>Glad to hear it!</b>

08:02.420 --> 08:07.130
<b>As long as you're happy, I'm happy!</b>

08:02.710 --> 08:06.830
Glad to hear it! As long as you're happy, I'm happy!

08:07.420 --> 08:10.790
S-smartphones are fun!

08:13.540 --> 08:19.250
<b>Glad to hear it!</b>

08:13.540 --> 08:19.250
<b>As long as you're happy, I'm happy!</b>

08:13.540 --> 08:19.250
<b>Miko,</b>

08:13.540 --> 08:19.250
<b>oh miko,</b>

08:13.550 --> 08:19.250
<b>right now I'm playing a</b>

08:13.550 --> 08:19.250
<b>nostalgic game on my smartphone</b>

08:14.040 --> 08:17.290
Miko, oh miko, right now I'm playing a nostalgic game

08:17.290 --> 08:18.630
on my smartphone.

08:21.710 --> 08:28.080
<b>Earlier, Tama from the Murai Flower</b>

08:21.710 --> 08:28.080
<b>Shop came to our garden.</b>

08:21.710 --> 08:28.080
<b>He was so cute,</b>

08:21.710 --> 08:28.080
<b>miko</b>

08:22.000 --> 08:26.960
Earlier, Tama from the Murai Flower Shop
came to our garden. He was so cute, miko.

08:28.080 --> 08:30.250
<b>Oh, miko...</b>

08:28.080 --> 08:30.250
<b>I don't know the answer</b>

08:28.090 --> 08:30.250
<b>to this crossword.</b>

08:28.090 --> 08:30.250
<b>Seven characters,</b>

08:28.090 --> 08:30.250
<b>and the first one is "mi"</b>

08:28.710 --> 08:29.670
Oh, miko...

08:30.920 --> 08:35.500
I don't know the answer to this crossword.
Seven characters, and the first one is "mi."

08:43.290 --> 08:48.630
I... may have created a horrible monster.

08:48.630 --> 08:53.000
I'm going home before I get caught up in this.
See ya. Best of luck.

08:53.380 --> 08:56.330
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

08:56.880 --> 08:58.830
U-um, say, Elda...

08:59.250 --> 08:59.920
Hmm?

09:00.170 --> 09:03.290
About the smartphone,
you're kinda sending a lot of texts...

09:03.580 --> 09:09.040
Th-that's right! It's so much more fun
than I anticipated, I end up sending tons of them!

09:09.460 --> 09:14.170
The stamps you send me are fun,
and smartphones are fun!

09:14.540 --> 09:16.210
She put stickers on it...

09:16.630 --> 09:19.290
O-oh neat, that's great.

09:20.210 --> 09:22.830
Speaking of, how are the spirits doing?
What's going on with them?

09:22.960 --> 09:29.130
Oh, well, they don't come to me when I call them.
I suppose that's fine now that I have this.

09:34.540 --> 09:39.500
<b>In the middle of the night</b>

09:34.540 --> 09:39.500
<b>I start craving cup ramen</b>

09:34.540 --> 09:39.500
<b>What about you, miko?</b>

09:39.500 --> 09:41.380
S-send.

09:55.250 --> 09:57.290
She isn't responding.

10:11.920 --> 10:14.790
Koito... Koito...

10:17.630 --> 10:20.670
Koito... Koito...

10:28.460 --> 10:29.960
E-Elda?!

10:30.170 --> 10:32.960
Y-You scared me! Don't burst out a scream like that!

10:32.960 --> 10:34.210
That's what I should be saying!

10:34.420 --> 10:36.580
Why are you here in the middle of the night?!

10:37.670 --> 10:38.830
I texted you.

10:42.580 --> 10:43.920
This isn't working.

10:44.130 --> 10:48.540
I have to do something
about this smartphone monster I've created!

10:49.500 --> 10:53.920
H-hey, Elda. This is hard to say,
but it turns out the smartphone is-

10:55.500 --> 10:57.500
Wh-what is this light?!

11:01.750 --> 11:05.210
S-spirits. My spirits are back!

11:05.670 --> 11:09.500
<b>What's up, suckers?</b>

11:08.040 --> 11:09.210
Th-they've gone astray!

11:09.500 --> 11:11.960
<b>What's up, suckers?</b>

11:09.670 --> 11:11.830
Wha...? Is that what you call this?!

11:11.960 --> 11:17.920
<b>What's up, suckers?</b>

11:12.130 --> 11:17.210
Th-they're glowing like a neon light.
What's wrong, spirits?

11:17.960 --> 11:23.130
Could they be sulking because you've only
been using your smartphone to send messages?

11:25.130 --> 11:27.830
I-is that true, spirits?

11:28.000 --> 11:30.960
<b>What's up, suckers?</b>

11:31.130 --> 11:35.420
I-I'm sorry, I'm so sorry, spirits!

11:38.670 --> 11:44.420
Koito, I don't need a smartphone after all.
I have my spirits.

11:44.960 --> 11:48.670
Yeah, yeah! You're right, Elda!

11:49.630 --> 11:53.250
And this is how Elda's addiction to smartphones
was somehow obscured

11:53.420 --> 11:55.960
in a somewhat touching atmosphere...

11:55.750 --> 11:59.960
<b>SEALED</b>

11:56.460 --> 11:59.040
and the spirits were completely healthy again.

12:00.500 --> 12:02.420
And then, I made an oath.

12:03.040 --> 12:07.460
I swore I'd never suggest that Elda
use a smartphone or anything again.

12:09.290 --> 12:13.040
Oh, miko... you will buy me a Red Bull
on your way home.

12:14.830 --> 12:17.250
You're the only one that ended up the loser here, huh?

12:21.040 --> 12:23.880
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

12:26.830 --> 12:29.290
<b>MELTY</b>

12:26.830 --> 12:29.290
<b>CHEESE</b>

12:26.840 --> 12:29.290
<b>SLICES</b>

12:37.630 --> 12:39.130
Yes, this hits the spot!

12:39.580 --> 12:45.630
A huge gob of ketchup on a thick piece of toast,
with melted cheese and greasy bacon!

12:45.880 --> 12:48.130
I want to eat this every now and then!

12:48.130 --> 12:51.580
But if Koito finds out then she'll be angry with me,
so I have it in secret.

12:48.630 --> 12:50.420
That leaves no room for dinner!

12:48.710 --> 12:51.670
<b>That leaves</b>

12:48.710 --> 12:51.670
<b>no room</b>

12:48.710 --> 12:51.670
<b>for dinner!</b>

12:51.670 --> 12:56.130
<b>Salted</b>

12:51.830 --> 12:55.630
I-I know! What if I crush the potato chips
and put those in?!

12:58.330 --> 13:01.460
It feels like a week's worth of daily calories!

13:01.580 --> 13:11.290
<b>Filet wrapped in pie crust</b>

13:01.580 --> 13:11.290
<b>Beef Wellington</b>

13:01.590 --> 13:11.290
<b>Hamburg steak</b>

13:01.590 --> 13:11.290
<b>Spicy Cod Roe</b>

13:01.590 --> 13:11.290
<b>Pasta</b>

13:01.630 --> 13:03.170
I apologize, Koyuzuko.

13:03.420 --> 13:06.130
Your daily meals are amazing,

13:06.130 --> 13:10.830
but please forgive me for the crime of wanting
to eat something sloppy like this occasionally.

13:13.830 --> 13:16.210
Oh... look what I've done.

13:16.670 --> 13:18.880
I guess I have to change now.

13:25.670 --> 13:28.540
Finally... I've finally got it.

13:29.130 --> 13:32.080
It's second-hand and was the cheapest one there, but...

13:32.460 --> 13:35.250
I finally have the mature-looking trenchcoat
I've been longing for!

13:35.960 --> 13:39.290
That's because you did your best to refrain
from buying snacks, huh, Koito?

13:39.500 --> 13:42.210
It's a pretty famous brand, right?

13:42.380 --> 13:43.080
Yup!

13:46.380 --> 13:49.170
What do you think, Koma-chan? Do I look good in it?

13:50.920 --> 13:54.250
Nope. Doesn't suit you at all!

13:55.040 --> 13:58.790
Oh, wait. Since it's already dirty,
I should finish eating first.

14:00.460 --> 14:01.790
I'm home, Elda.

14:02.790 --> 14:04.460
Koma-chan tagged along today.

14:08.580 --> 14:11.130
E-Elda! Th-there's blood...!

14:11.130 --> 14:13.960
A-ambulance! Ambulance!

14:13.960 --> 14:15.920
N-no. This isn't blood...

14:16.290 --> 14:19.210
I'm sorry. I was snacking between meals.

14:20.330 --> 14:22.540
Ah, you scared me!

14:22.790 --> 14:25.380
Oh, did you buy new clothes?

14:25.380 --> 14:27.630
Yup! Got a great deal on it, too!

14:27.960 --> 14:29.710
It doesn't look good on her, though.

14:29.960 --> 14:32.170
Why'd you buy something so baggy?

14:32.500 --> 14:34.250
This is something I'm gonna wear some day!

14:34.250 --> 14:36.540
It'll be my size when I'm 20!

14:36.920 --> 14:41.420
I'm sure I'll... no! I'll absolutely get taller!
You can do it, limbs!

14:42.170 --> 14:45.790
I do like that excessive positivity you've got, though.

14:46.420 --> 14:50.420
But I'm telling you, it suits you more when you go
for a casual style than a grown-up celebrity style.

14:50.670 --> 14:53.460
I do understand that you admire
the "Lady in White" though.

14:53.880 --> 14:57.750
"Lady in White"? Didn't you also mention
something about that before?

14:57.750 --> 14:59.420
D-don't worry about that!

14:59.580 --> 15:05.880
M-more importantly, the fee to get your garments clean!
I'm deducting the precise amount from your offerings!

15:05.880 --> 15:08.290
Huh? H-how cruel!

15:08.540 --> 15:11.210
Can't we use it as materials for amulets?!

15:11.210 --> 15:13.130
We can't use dirty ones for that.

15:13.290 --> 15:15.670
Eh, what do you mean by "materials for amulets"?

15:16.040 --> 15:21.670
Actually, the amulets from Takamimi Shrine have scraps
from divine imperial garments I've worn in them.

15:19.830 --> 15:21.170
<b>Divine Imperial Garments</b>

15:21.830 --> 15:34.960
<b>Takamimi Shrine</b>

15:21.920 --> 15:24.630
Oh really? I have one, too.

15:24.960 --> 15:28.830
This amulet is nice, right? It's got a good repuation
for being divinely blessed, too.

15:29.080 --> 15:32.790
Huh? It's divinely blessed? Even though I'm just an elf?!

15:33.040 --> 15:37.540
Yeah, after I prayed the other day and I bought
a peeno ice cream, there was a heart in it.

15:35.830 --> 15:37.540
Yay! All right! I got a heart!

15:37.580 --> 15:41.960
N-no fair! How come I never get any divine blessings?!

15:41.960 --> 15:44.630
What do you call all the
food and drink offerings you get then?!

15:45.000 --> 15:51.210
But speaking of Elda-sama's clothing,
you've always worn the same kind ever since I was a kid.

15:51.500 --> 15:53.130
Don't you have anything else?

15:54.540 --> 15:57.380
I-I have 20 more like this.

15:57.710 --> 15:59.380
Why are you bragging about that?

15:59.880 --> 16:02.250
Don't you ever want to wear something different?

16:02.250 --> 16:09.920
N-no, not really. When I was summoned here I didn't like
short sleeve kimono, but now I'm totally okay with it.

16:10.040 --> 16:14.000
Oh, I know! Let's have Elda try on this trenchcoat!

16:14.830 --> 16:17.580
That might be fun! Seems the size is just perfect, too!

16:17.830 --> 16:20.130
Uh, n-no, I don't really...

16:20.290 --> 16:22.380
Now come on, don't say that!

16:22.500 --> 16:23.710
Uh...

16:30.130 --> 16:33.750
H-huh? Somehow it doesn't really suit you.

16:34.500 --> 16:36.670
There are woodblock prints of monsters
that look like this...

16:37.210 --> 16:41.830
Hmm. Elda-sama, stand up straighter. Like this!

16:42.040 --> 16:43.250
U-um?

16:43.250 --> 16:44.170
Straighter!

16:44.170 --> 16:45.460
Eh? Like this?

16:46.250 --> 16:48.540
Then play with the hair a little bit...

16:49.000 --> 16:50.080
How does it look now?

17:00.920 --> 17:02.420
Are we in Paris?

17:03.250 --> 17:06.500
Whoa! You look super cool, Elda-sama!

17:06.880 --> 17:09.540
O-oh? I-I can't really tell...

17:12.170 --> 17:15.670
Smartphone camera, turn on!

17:17.290 --> 17:20.710
Dang it, dang it, dang it!

17:21.000 --> 17:22.420
K-Koito?

17:24.670 --> 17:26.290
A-Are we done?

17:26.710 --> 17:29.170
I think I like my normal clothes better.

17:30.290 --> 17:30.880
Huh?

17:34.670 --> 17:38.330
S-sorry Koito. Are you okay?

17:45.130 --> 17:48.500
<b>Click Click Click Click Click Click Click</b>

17:46.710 --> 17:47.960
K-Koito?!

17:54.880 --> 17:57.380
Y-You okay, Koito?

17:57.960 --> 17:59.670
I-I'm fine.

18:00.130 --> 18:02.580
Elda is really something from up close.

18:02.960 --> 18:06.580
Elda-sama, you're beautiful so you should wear
more fashionable clothes.

18:06.830 --> 18:09.380
U-um, but you know...

18:09.750 --> 18:12.830
I would hate to be arrested for looking too fashionable.

18:12.830 --> 18:14.580
A-arrested?

18:14.710 --> 18:18.960
I-I mean, it was a thing in the Edo days,
a ban on being fashion-conscious.

18:19.420 --> 18:22.920
The stylishness of feudal lords' clothing
became a way to compete with each other.

18:23.130 --> 18:26.460
Showy and luxurious items steadily became popular.

18:26.830 --> 18:32.080
And then, the shogunate established an
"extravagance ban" that prohibited flashy clothing.

18:32.170 --> 18:37.880
<b>No extravagance allowed.</b>

18:32.170 --> 18:37.880
<b>Shogunate</b>

18:32.420 --> 18:35.250
Only subdued colors allowed to be used in kimono.

18:35.250 --> 18:36.920
<b>Extravagance Ban</b>

18:35.420 --> 18:37.710
Bright patterns were also prohibited.

18:38.170 --> 18:40.630
I didn't know that... That sucks.

18:41.040 --> 18:45.380
But that did nothing to stop
everyone's passion for fashion.

18:45.540 --> 18:49.920
They made the patterns in great detail
so that from a distance they looked plain.

18:50.170 --> 18:54.880
<b>It has</b>

18:50.170 --> 18:54.880
<b>a pattern!</b>

18:50.210 --> 18:50.830
It has a pattern!

18:50.920 --> 18:54.210
And that Edo-komon is still cherished today.

18:55.170 --> 18:59.580
So people used legal loopholes
for the sake of fashion, huh? Amazing.

18:55.960 --> 18:57.790
<b>Edo-komon</b>

18:59.880 --> 19:04.500
They also did a lot of other things,
such as making an elaborate hem on a kimono,

19:04.500 --> 19:07.330
or making the kimono flutter in a neat way.

19:07.580 --> 19:09.880
The Edo-komon is especially interesting.

19:10.170 --> 19:13.460
There's the high-class ceremonial dress
samurai use called "kamishimo-komon,"

19:11.670 --> 19:13.170
<b>Kamishimo-komon</b>

19:13.580 --> 19:16.880
and the "iware-komon,"
born from the culture of the townspeople.

19:15.130 --> 19:16.380
<b>Iware-komon</b>

19:17.040 --> 19:18.540
<b>Seven Dieties of Luck</b>

19:17.380 --> 19:22.330
In "iware-komon," auspicious patterns
and witty jokes and the like were favored.

19:22.330 --> 19:25.040
<b>Peaceful and Prosperous Home</b>

19:22.540 --> 19:25.670
Like the fine patterns for long life and fortune,
and for a peaceful and prosperous home...

19:25.880 --> 19:29.790
There's also sea bream and small mallets,
and even grated daikon radish patterns.

19:27.000 --> 19:30.250
<b>Daikon and</b>

19:27.000 --> 19:30.250
<b>daikon grater</b>

19:30.250 --> 19:33.830
Oh! I'd like to try a Nin***do pattern, I think.

19:33.830 --> 19:35.250
That'd be wonderful!

19:35.500 --> 19:39.380
You shouldn't, people would get angry with you
even in modern times for that.

19:44.080 --> 19:47.830
Seeing something like this makes me lose confidence...

19:48.040 --> 19:51.330
And I was thinking of wearing this coat
at the Coming of Age ceremony, too.

19:51.500 --> 19:55.380
Hm? Were you wanting clothes to wear
to the Coming of Age ceremony?

19:55.750 --> 19:58.210
Huh? Y-yeah, kind of...

20:02.540 --> 20:05.170
C-can you two turn away for a moment?

20:05.420 --> 20:06.580
What? Why?

20:06.790 --> 20:11.500
I-I'm going to open my closet!
I'm embarrassed for you to see what's in my closet!

20:15.040 --> 20:17.960
Let's see... Where'd I put it...?

20:18.460 --> 20:23.000
Is it this box? Oh, no, this is the *C Engine.

20:23.500 --> 20:28.790
This box? Ah, this is the C*-romrom. Huh?

20:30.040 --> 20:32.170
Ah, found it! Here it is!

20:32.420 --> 20:35.080
What is it? What is she doing now?

20:35.080 --> 20:36.670
N-no idea.

20:37.040 --> 20:40.000
O-okay, you can turn around now!

21:02.380 --> 21:06.000
It's the Takamimi Shrine's miko furisode,
passed down through generations.

21:06.380 --> 21:11.630
It's a little different from the coat
you wanted to wear, but... will this one do?

21:15.500 --> 21:23.170
My mom, and my mom's mom,
and her mother, too... They all wore this furisode?

21:23.500 --> 21:24.960
Yes, that's right.

21:25.420 --> 21:28.380
I-I can wear it, too?

21:29.000 --> 21:32.290
Of course. Want to try it on?

21:48.380 --> 21:52.420
How is it, Koma-chan? Does it... suit me?

21:53.630 --> 21:58.580
Yeah! It really does! I'm gonna take some pics!

21:59.040 --> 22:00.670
Yeah, please take some!

22:00.880 --> 22:03.420
Okay, the shoji screen will be the background.

22:03.420 --> 22:04.880
Now, strike a pose.

22:04.880 --> 22:06.210
L-like this?

22:17.880 --> 22:21.250
Don't rush into becoming an adult, okay?

22:21.790 --> 22:23.960
Huh? What'd you say, Elda?

22:24.130 --> 22:25.000
Nothing.

22:25.250 --> 22:30.250
B-by the way, now will you forget
about taking money away from my offering?

22:30.500 --> 22:31.460
I will not!

22:31.710 --> 22:34.210
Such cruelty!

22:41.960 --> 22:43.210
Koma-chan! Koma-chan!

22:45.960 --> 22:49.250
I think I'm going to aim for these
awesome high heels next!

22:49.420 --> 22:51.580
Even if I don't grow, this will be a good option!

22:51.830 --> 22:57.960
<b>Great condition! Italian-made High-heels! With box</b>

22:53.460 --> 22:57.000
I also love that you never seem to learn your lesson...
